(1) of any investigation or proceeding into or relating to an offence by any person ,under this Act or of a to commit, or an attempt to commit, or an abetment of any such offence, the Public Prosecutor may by

(a) any such person to furnish a statutory all movable or immovable belonging to or possessed by such person and by the spouse and children of such person, and the date on which each of the properties was acquired and whether it was acquired by way of purchase, gift, bequest, inheritance or otherwIse;

(b) any such person to furnish a statutory of any money or other property paid or disposed of by him during such period as may be the order;

(c) any other person to furnish a statutory all movable or immovable belonging to or possessed by such person the Public Prosecutor has reasonable grounds to believe that such information may be relevant to the or proceedings;

(d) the Collector of Income Tax to furnish all information to the Collector relating to the affairs of such person or of the spouse or child of such person and to produce or furnish, specified in the notice, any document or a certified copy of any relating to such person or the spouse or child of such person wllich is in the possession or under the control of such Collector;

(e) the person in charge of any department, office or establishment of the Government, or the president, chairman, manager or chief executive of any public body to produce or furnish as in the notice, any document or a certified copy of any document which is in his possession or his control;

(j) the manager of any bank to give copies of such person or of the spouse or child of such person at the bank.

(2) Every person to whom an order is given by the Prosecutor under subsection (1) of this section shall, notwithstanding the provisions of any written law or any oath the contrary, comply with the terms of the order such time as may be specified therein and any person who wilfully neglects or fails so to comply shall be guilty of an shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding to imprisonment for a term not exceeding one year or to both such fine and imprisonment.
